From 318b3084c7150233e88865b6442c1c56d5b6a2ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:17:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] drtm: parse event logs by advertised digest size

DEN0113 1.4B section 3.17.1 (R316020) requires the DRTM event log to
follow the crypto agile event log structure from the TCG PC Client
Platform Firmware Profile Specification, whose TCG_PCR_EVENT2 records
store their TPML_DIGEST_VALUES densely: each digest is a two-byte
algorithm ID followed by a digest whose size is advertised by the
Specification ID event, not an array of fixed-size TPMT_HA objects.

dl006 and dl012 incorrectly cast the digest list to an ACS TPMT_HA whose
digest member was hard-coded to SHA256_DIGEST_SIZE. Against a conformant
implementation that enables SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-384, and SHA-512 banks,
this made every entry appear to have a 34-byte stride. After the first
digest, subsequent algorithm IDs were read from digest bytes. The
calculated event-data pointer consequently landed inside the SHA-512
digest, and those bytes were interpreted as eventSize. dl006 then
attempted to print that bogus, extremely large payload and appeared to
hang while reading beyond the event record. dl012 used the same invalid
stepping when searching for its DLME event.

The existing shared event-log helpers were not safe replacements as
written. Initialization dereferenced the DLME data header before proving
that it fit in the region, omitted dlme_data_offset from a region
calculation, used overflow-prone additions, and did not fully validate the
legacy Spec ID record. Event iteration bounded fields against the whole
log instead of the current record, trusted digest counts and eventSize,
allowed duplicate algorithms, and treated a zero record as normal
termination. Digest lookup was likewise able to walk beyond the digest
list. The helper also rejected SHA-1 even though SHA-1 remains valid as an
enabled event-log bank.

Harden initialization and iteration with subtraction-based bounds checks,
canonical algorithm sizes, duplicate detection, exact Spec ID and vendor
data sizing, explicit payload lengths, and packed wire structures for
unaligned Event2 records. Keep SHA-1 support local to event-log parsing so
it does not relax the DRTM TCB hash APIs.

Convert dl006 and dl012 to the audited iterator. For the DCE event,
require exactly one digest for every enabled bank and separately validate
that event data is a TPMT_HA encoded with the selected firmware hash
algorithm and its exact digest length, per DEN0113 1.4B section
4.8.2 (event data is "a TPMT_HA structure with value of DCE_digest
... densely packed based on the size of the digest without
padding"). Remove numeric comparisons between TPM algorithm identifiers
and the unbounded raw payload print.

This fixes test 106 against a conformant implementation's mixed
SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-384/SHA-512 event log and prevents malformed lengths or
offsets from turning parser failures into out-of-bounds walks or hangs.

Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
